<title>SAUDI ARABIA: Saudi social security invests $666mln in 46 firms.</title>
<headline>Saudi social security invests $666mln in 46 firms.</headline>
<dateline>RIYADH 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's General Organisation for Social Insurance (GOSI) has invested more than 2.5 billion riyals in 46 Saudi companies, the Saudi Press Agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The agency said GOSI, the state's social security arm, had paid out 17.5 billion riyals to its members. It gave no timeframe.</p>
<p>SPA said more than 2.5 million people were registered with GOSI, set up in 1969, and more than 98 percent of them were Saudis.</p>
</text>
